WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.890
- Did you ever feel like
you were loved as a child?

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:04.120
- No.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.953
No.

00:00:04.953 --> 00:00:06.240
And because I had never had been

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.680
I didn't really miss it either.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.140
You know, I really

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.423
to this day I probably still
don't know what love is.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:16.850
- All right, BJ.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.683
- Yes.

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:18.810
BJ, where are you from originally?

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.643
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:19.643 --> 00:00:20.650
- I grew up in Hollywood

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.830
and I've been in San
Francisco for like 30 years.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:24.663
- Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:24.663 --> 00:00:25.550
You had both your parents

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.270
growing up as a child.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.240
- I had no family growing up.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.334
- Where were your folks?

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:31.290
- I have no idea.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.010
I still don't know them.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.730
- So you never knew your parents?

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:35.563
- No.

00:00:35.563 --> 00:00:36.396
- Who raised you?

00:00:36.396 --> 00:00:38.633
- I grew up pretty much in juvenile hall.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.670
I'd go in and out of foster homes but

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:43.910
something bad always happened

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.090
and I always ended up
back in juvenile hall.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.550
So juvenile hall became home to me.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.170
And after awhile I got to where that's

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.150
where I wanted it to be.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.430
You know, everybody else
will go to juvenile hall and

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.230
run away to get out.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.760
I used to run away from
foster homes to go back

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.850
to juvenile hall because
it was where I knew,

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.153
where I was comfortable.

00:01:05.051 --> 00:01:06.209
- What kind of childhood did you have?

00:01:06.209 --> 00:01:07.459
How would you describe it

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.413
- Alone.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.250
Very unstable.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.450
I was never in any one place

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.193
for more than two or three months.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.600
- Did you have any
traumatic events as a kid or

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.433
any abuse?

00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:22.266
Anything like that?

00:01:22.266 --> 00:01:23.099
- Yeah.

00:01:23.099 --> 00:01:26.573
I got thrown through a wall
one time for wetting the bed.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.090
I was thrown from the bedroom

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.750
all the way through the
wall into the living room

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.080
because I wet the bed.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.390
I was like eight years
old and I wet the bed

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.400
and the foster family
didn't like that too much.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.755
And I had one foster
family that the only reason

00:01:42.755 --> 00:01:46.010
they even had any foster
kids were so they had

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.680
somebody to beat on

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:50.120
and they used to beat us mercilessly

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.503
for no reason, pretty much every day.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.810
And most of the foster
homes that I ended up in

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.460
they only had us there
so they could get paid

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.190
cause they get paid a certain amount

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:02.950
of money for each kid they have.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.880
And some of the foster homes had like

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:08.150
eight, 10, 12 kids that
they didn't care about.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:09.550
It was just about the money.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.880
So I mean,

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.780
I had a good childhood

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.420
in the sense that

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:17.523
I didn't have any,

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.000
anybody telling me

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.480
if you don't finish your
dinner you gotta go to bed,

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.620
but at the same time,

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.840
I didn't have anybody telling me

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.144
here's your dinner, enjoy it.

00:02:31.144 --> 00:02:32.320
(chuckles) You know?

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.470
I didn't even know if I was
going to have something to eat

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.303
or not.

00:02:35.303 --> 00:02:37.380
- Did you ever feel like
you were loved as a child?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.630
- No.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:39.463
No.

00:02:39.463 --> 00:02:40.740
And because I had never had been

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.190
I didn't really miss it either.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:43.680
You know, I really

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.707
to this day I probably still
don't know what love is.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.020
I believe I'm starting to love myself.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.220
I haven't been locked up in over 20 years.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.560
This is the best I've
ever had my life together.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.420
You know?

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.930
I've got a permanent
place to live, I pay rent.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:01.960
I've got

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:02.793
TV.

00:03:02.793 --> 00:03:04.408
I've got a

00:03:04.408 --> 00:03:05.241
nice room.

00:03:05.241 --> 00:03:07.483
About everything in my room
is bought and paid for.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:12.030
I've got a nice towel, a
nice entertainment center,

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.530
three cats who love me.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.420
- This is the best point
in your life so far?

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.253
- Yeah.

00:03:16.253 --> 00:03:17.086
- How old are you?

00:03:17.086 --> 00:03:17.919
- 62.

00:03:17.919 --> 00:03:18.940
- 62?

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:19.773
- Yeah.

00:03:19.773 --> 00:03:21.830
- And what was the worst
point in your life?

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.113
- LA County jail.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.980
- What were you in jail for?

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.110
- These pills and prescriptions,
doctors prescriptions

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.360
for different drugs in Hollywood.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.560
And for a white boy to
go into LA County jail

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:40.450
with swastikas all over
him, oh, it was ugly.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.440
Every time my door got
open for dinner or shower

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.690
or anything, at least three
black guys would rush in my cell

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.490
and beat the dog shell out of me.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:51.923
Every time I saw a guy open that happened.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.610
And there was nothing I could do about it.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:57.720
I was the only white
boy on the whole terror.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.260
That was the ugliest time of
my life that I can remember.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.370
- Tell me about the swastika
tattoos on your chest and arm.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:05.451
- I went to prison,

00:04:05.451 --> 00:04:07.670
I went to Tracy when I was 17.

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:09.550
and at that time Tracy was

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:11.820
it was called the gladiator school.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:15.050
It was where the really
rough cases started out.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:16.445
They would go to Tracy and

00:04:16.445 --> 00:04:19.200
learn how to be a convict
and then go from there

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.400
to either San Joaquin or Folsom.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.870
And I went in a pretty boy from Hollywood,

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.230
17 years old

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:29.103
and I was stabbed.

00:04:29.103 --> 00:04:31.620
And I didn't wanna get raped

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.920
and I didn't wanna have
my shit taken from me.

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:38.160
I was offered an opportunity to ship

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:39.280
up with Aaron brotherhood.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.850
I was told, you're white

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:42.390
you know,

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.280
be with us,

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.113
stay with us.

00:04:44.113 --> 00:04:45.110
We'll take care of you,

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.740
teach you everything you need to know,

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.620
give anything you need to have.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.890
And I did.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.120
And I never got jumped

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.993
or beat up by the blacks at all.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:56.530
But I had to participate in their mess

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.910
in order to do that.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:02.400
I would have to carry weapons
and stab people in the yard.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.480
And anytime anything jumped off

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:06.330
between whites and the any other race

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.640
if I was there and didn't get involved,

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.990
then they would beat the
hell out of me for it.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.870
So, I mean, it had its pros
and cons, but I survived.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.653
I did what I had to to survive.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.230
I'm not a racists

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.910
I don't have a lot of black friends.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:25.390
I am a little bit prejudiced, but

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:28.750
the same thing that I
hate black people for

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.170
if white people were doing it

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.130
I hate them for it too.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:32.963
It's this

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.980
negative mentality.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.430
That's all I can say is that's what it is.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:39.360
And I don't like any

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.210
whites, blacks, greens,
purples, or any of they.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:46.010
I appear to be a lot more prejudice

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:48.913
than I am because mostly I vow round that.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:52.220
But plus I've gotten to where,

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.440
like I said I'm pleased with my life,

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:55.670
I don't bother anybody,

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.900
I don't let anybody bother me.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.540
I do my thing and

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.213
go my way.

00:06:01.213 --> 00:06:04.210
You know, I'm not trying to
interrupt you or bother you

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.360
and I'm not going to
let you do that to me.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:10.700
- How many years have you
lived in the Tenderloin,

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:11.760
In San Francisco?

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.660
- I've been in San Francisco
for 30 or 35 years, about.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.580
- And you've been homeless for how long?

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:18.413
- Until

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:23.250
like 22 years ago I was always homeless.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.820
- And now you're staying in one of the...

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.653
- I'm in the

00:06:27.032 --> 00:06:29.280
SRO, the mission hotel

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.063
and it's in the mission district actually.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.860
- Did you come down here for...

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.910
- I came down here to get my check.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.150
I have my pays off.

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:39.850
This is right where we're standing

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:41.700
and that's where I pick up my check.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:42.720
- That's where I found you.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:43.750
- Yeah.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:45.790
- Do you use any of the
drugs that are on the street?

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:47.400
- I use heroin.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.950
- How long have you used heroin?

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:49.783
- About

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:51.503
10 years.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:53.293
Yeah.

00:06:53.293 --> 00:06:54.126
And I don't get high,

00:06:54.126 --> 00:06:55.830
I just maintain.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.790
I shoot three times a day
just to be functional,

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.273
I get sick if I don't do it.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:03.910
- And how do you support yourself?

00:07:04.975 --> 00:07:05.880
- Through the SSI

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.360
Plus I'm an artist.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.420
I draw a lot of pictures

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.200
for a lot of people and

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:14.380
different things present itself.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:18.700
You know, there's people
that just find stern

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.960
and they'd look at me and,

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.170
hey will you escorting me to go shopping

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.570
or will you escort me to pick
up my check or wait around.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.720
I usually get paid $50 for that.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.343
And that happens two
or three times a week.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.100
- Have you ever been in love before?

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.133
- I don't think so.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.750
- And you have no kids?

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:39.583
- No.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:42.370
No. I won't have any kids either.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:44.790
I mean what kind of father would I be?

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.600
Yeah.(chuckling)

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:47.433
No.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:48.470
- Do you have friends?

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:50.289
- Do I have friends?

00:07:50.289 --> 00:07:52.110
I have acquaintances.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.300
I don't think I have anybody
that I would call a friend

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:55.133
right now.

00:07:55.133 --> 00:07:56.340
I'm not that close with anybody

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.860
and I don't wanna be cause

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:02.730
every time I've been
really hurt, bullied bad

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:07.180
it's been by somebody that
was really close to me.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.013
So,

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:12.030
and to say the truth I don't
feel like I need anybody

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:12.863
for anything.

00:08:12.863 --> 00:08:14.806
I take care of myself just fine.

00:08:14.806 --> 00:08:15.639
- Yeah.

00:08:15.639 --> 00:08:16.690
- So um,

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:18.803
all the shit that comes with a friendship,

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:20.663
I don't need it

00:08:20.663 --> 00:08:21.760
don't want it.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:22.593
Aint got time for it.

00:08:22.593 --> 00:08:24.193
- Given the lack of love that you had

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:27.220
throughout your life

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:28.720
how do you attribute the fact

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.170
that you're at your very best point

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:32.003
right now?

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:34.690
- Um,

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.110
the hard thing

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.580
getting me housed

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:41.180
once I got housed my life has been

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:42.013
so much better.

00:08:42.013 --> 00:08:43.600
I'm happy now.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:44.910
You know, once I got to

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.520
where I had a permanent place to live,

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.630
I'm not just here for a week or a month,

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.700
this is my home forever.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:53.313
When that happened, my whole life changed.

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:56.550
- Yeah. They seem like
a great organization.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:57.383
- Yeah.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:02.030
And there's so much
difference having an address

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:04.400
and having that stability.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:05.233
That's what it is,

00:09:05.233 --> 00:09:07.160
the stability.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.290
And living up to the responsibility

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:11.470
of having a place to
live, it's kinda nice.

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:13.650
You know, yeah it mean you can

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:16.470
be put in a place to live

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:20.380
and just be so irresponsible
you fuck it of, you know.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.397
And I don't do that either.

00:09:22.397 --> 00:09:23.230
You know.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.030
So I do appreciate what I've got

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.050
and I respect what I've got.

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:28.730
- Do you find having a
little responsibility

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.870
in your life gives your life meaning?

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:31.780
- Yeah.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:32.613
Yeah.

00:09:32.613 --> 00:09:33.940
- And the lack of responsibility

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.340
makes your life meaningless?

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.210
- Yeah.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:37.400
- And plus the things

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:40.050
of the day initially felt like
I've accomplished something.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:43.140
It's not just another wasted day.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.400
You know.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:45.438
And that kind of means something

00:09:45.438 --> 00:09:47.440
because I don't want to be worthless.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.290
You know, I don't want to
get in the way I want to be

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:51.680
in line late,

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:54.710
but I don't want to just exist either.

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:57.380
Yeah. I don't wanna lose worth.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.070
I have some value

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.615
to other people other than myself.

00:10:01.615 --> 00:10:04.215
- Do you have hope of getting
off of heroin one day?

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:07.900
- Yeah. I've been off of it twice

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:09.910
and I started using it again

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:12.350
not because I needed the drug

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:15.780
because I was bored to death.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:17.560
There was nothing else for me to do.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:20.480
I chase the bag all day
while I'm on it but I do.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:22.470
And if I'm not doing that,

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.830
there's nothing left.(chuckles)

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:27.830
It sad as it is to have to admit
this, there's nothing left.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:30.400
I've checked twice

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.643
and went back to using out of boredom.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.510
- What's the most important
lesson you've learned in your

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:38.360
interesting life?

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.900
Just the fact that you
grew up without love

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:47.650
gives you a very interesting
